    },
    {
      "title": "The Neoclassical Monopoly Paradox",
      "description": "Javier Milei analyzes how rapid post-1800 economic growth generated increasing returns, implying monopolies and concentrated structures under traditional neoclassical theory. Because neoclassical theory views monopolies as detrimental, Milei recognized a theoretical contradiction when observing that these same structures coincided with extreme poverty dropping from 95% to under 10% and middle-income individuals living better than Roman emperors."
    }
  ],
